   "interpretations": {
    "extraction_status": "extracted",
    "value": [
     "Reduced conscientiousness was associated with grey matter loss in the right premotor cortex and with relative preservation of grey matter in the left posterior superior temporal sulcus and superior temporal gyrus, as well as the left middle, inferior temporal and fusiform gyri and left central sulcus. The most robust neuroanatomical correlate of personality change was the association of decreased conscientiousness with relative grey matter preservation in the region of the left superior temporal sulcus and superior temporal gyrus."
    ],
    "value_source": "reported",
    "evidence": {
     "status": "present",
     "sets": [
      {
       "source": "model_quote",
       "spans": [
        {
         "text": "Reduced conscientiousness was associated with grey matter loss in\n right premotor cortex (  P  <0.001 uncorrected) and associated with\n relative preservation of grey matter in left posterior superior temporal\n sulcus and superior temporal gyrus (  P  <0.05 false discovery rate\n corrected over the whole brain volume when analysed in a trait-specific\n design;   P  <0.001 uncorrected after covarying for other personality\n traits), left middle, inferior temporal and fusiform gyri and left central\n sulcus (all   P  <0.001 uncorrected).",
